<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Webi River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Webi River was a late sixteenth-century engagement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> in which the Adalite leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-nasir">Muhammad ibn Nasir</a> was killed. Together with Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarsa-dengel">Sarsa Dengel</a>'s defeat and execution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-v-of-adal">Sultan Muhammad V</a> in 1577, it permanently ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> as a military power. The sultanate afterwards fragmented into city-state remnants.</p></div>
